* 
what happens internally when spring boot application  starts?

🔹 1. main() method is executed
SpringApplication.run(MyApplication.class, args);

What happens:
JVM starts
SpringApplication object is created
👉 Interview line:
Application starts from the main method using SpringApplication.run().

🔹 2. Application type is determined
Spring Boot checks:
Is it a web application?
Is it Servlet-based, Reactive, or Non-web?

Based on classpath:
spring-web → Servlet app
spring-webflux → Reactive app

👉 Interview line:
Spring Boot identifies the application type based on classpath.

🔹 3. Environment is prepared
Spring Boot:
Loads application.properties / application.yml
Reads command-line arguments
Sets active profiles (dev, test, prod)

👉 Interview line:
Spring Boot prepares the environment and loads configuration properties.

🔹 4. Banner is displayed

Default Spring Boot banner is printed
Can be customized or disabled
(Not critical, but often asked)

🔹 5. ApplicationContext is created
Based on application type:

AnnotationConfigServletWebServerApplicationContext (web)
AnnotationConfigApplicationContext (non-web)

👉 Interview line:
Spring creates the appropriate ApplicationContext.

🔹 6. Bean definitions are loaded

Spring Boot:
Scans packages (@ComponentScan)
Finds beans (@Component, @Service, @Repository, @Controller)
Loads configuration classes (@Configuration)

👉 Interview line:
Spring scans and registers all bean definitions.

🔹 7. Auto-configuration is applied

Spring Boot:
Uses @EnableAutoConfiguration
Reads spring.factories
Configures beans automatically (DataSource, JPA, Security, etc.)
Example:
If MySQL is present → configures DataSource
If Spring MVC is present → configures DispatcherServlet

👉 Interview line:
Spring Boot auto-configures beans based on classpath and properties.

🔹 8. Embedded server is started
Embedded Tomcat (default) starts
Server binds to configured port (8080 by default)

👉 Interview line:
Embedded web server is started automatically.

🔹 9. Beans are instantiated & dependency injection happens
Beans are created
Dependencies injected (@Autowired)
Bean lifecycle methods executed

👉 Interview line:
Spring creates beans and performs dependency injection.

🔹 10. ApplicationRunner / CommandLineRunner executed
If present:
CommandLineRunner
ApplicationRunner

They run after context initialization.

👉 Interview line:
Startup logic is executed using runners.

🔹 11. Application is ready to serve requests
Context is fully initialized
Controllers are mapped
App listens for HTTP requests

👉 Interview line:
Application is now ready to handle client requests.

🧠 One-Minute Interview Summary (Memorize This)
When a Spring Boot application starts, the main method calls SpringApplication.run(). 
Spring Boot determines the application type from classpath means from dependencies from pom.xml, prepares the environment and loads the configuration file, creates the ApplicationContext, scans and registers beans, 
applies auto-configuration, starts the embedded server, performs dependency injection, and finally makes the application ready to serve requests.


